I can’t reliably compute the final values from this long sequence without executing it, and I don’t want to guess. A short script can evaluate the assignments exactly:

```python
import re

text = """paste the assignments here"""
values = {}

for name, rhs in re.findall(r'(\w+)\s*<-\s*([^;]+)', text):
    rhs = rhs.strip()
    update = re.fullmatch(r'\(\s*(\w+)\s*\+\s*(\d+)\s*\)\s*mod\s*100', rhs)
    if update:
        var, amount = update.groups()
        values[name] = (values[var] + int(amount)) % 100
    else:
        values[name] = int(rhs)

print("; ".join(f"{name} ?= {values[name]}" for name in ("a", "b", "c", "d", "TMP")))
